  "body": "## Summary\n\nTwo smartcopy bugs, both reproducible with `ffmpeg` and `mediamolder run` alone:\n\n1. **Re-encoded boundary GOPs did not decode** (H.264 and HEVC, MP4 and MOV). Boundary packets were forwarded as Annex B, referring to the encoder's own SPS/PPS, while the track kept the source's avcC/hvcC. Decoders read the start codes as NAL lengths and parsed the slices against the wrong parameter sets, so every re-encoded frame was dropped or garbled.\n2. **Open-GOP sources lost in-window frames.** GOPs were grouped in decode order, so a GOP's leading pictures (displayed before its keyframe) were dropped at both cuts.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Re-encoded packets are re-framed to the source's NAL framing (length-prefixed for avcC/hvcC sources).\n- **H.264 + libx264:** the boundary encoder takes a free `sps-id`; its SPS/PPS are appended to the output avcC. Track stays `avc1`, copied packets byte-identical.\n- **HEVC, and H.264 with other encoders:** parameter sets travel in-band, the source's VPS/SPS/PPS are re-inserted on copied keyframes, and MP4/MOV outputs get `hev1` / `avc3`. Applied on both sink stream-registration paths.\n- GOPs are classified by presentation span; consecutive boundary GOPs form one re-encoded run; the leading pictures of the copied GOP after a head cut join that run.\n- Splices: CRA→BLA for HEVC; for H.264 the copied slices' `pic_order_cnt_lsb` and `frame_num` are shifted in place until the next IDR (fixed-width fields, slice data untouched). Without this libavcodec reorders or drops frames at the head cut on open-GOP x264 sources.\n- Re-encoded packets carry durations and display-order DTS (the MP4 edit list otherwise cut the run's last frame; DTS collisions at joins made movenc reject packets). The boundary encoder's B-frame depth and reference count are kept within the source's.\n- `smartcopy_global_header` is ignored; the GUI toggle is removed (embedded bundle rebuilt).\n- Docs: `docs/smartcopy.md` \"How it works\" and limitations; CHANGELOG entry.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `job/handlers_smartcopy_cut_test.go`: generated 64×64 fixtures (80 frames, GOP 12, two B-frames) for H.264/HEVC, open/closed GOP, MP4/MOV. Cuts are decoded with the stream's own extradata and checked for frame count, order, content and `decode_error_flags`; plus a cut-position sweep over open-GOP sources and an in-band H.264 run with `h264_videotoolbox` (skips where unavailable).\n- `job/smartcopy_nal_test.go`: NAL framing, avcC/hvcC, CRA→BLA, RBSP escaping, prefix-overflow refusal.\n- `go test ./...`, `go vet`, frontend `tsc`/lint, `make build-gui-static` pass.\n\n## Known residuals\n\n- Open-GOP H.264: a head cut within a few frames of a non-IDR keyframe can make libavcodec log `mmco: unref short failure` (copied slices' MMCO ops address pictures before the cut); the decode is correct.\n- AVFoundation playback of `hev1` / multi-SPS avcC is not verified.\n",
